 ],
 "extraction_notes": "The main article provides one plotted 50 h stability series for each of PtGa/SiO2, PtGa-Pb/SiO2, and Pt3Sn/SiO2, plus textual summaries of the 96 h PtGa-Pb run, the 650 °C PtGa-Pb run, and the Ga/SiO2 control. Stability curves were represented as one record per catalyst/run using their first and last reported or plotted conversions, in accordance with the stability-run rule. Exact printed initial values supersede plot readings. The 96 h PtGa-Pb result is reported as 30% conversion and 99.6% selectivity without performance loss. No propylene formation rates, yields, or numerical deactivation constants are provided in the supplied main-paper material. The computed H2/C3H8 molar ratio is 5.0/3.9; no other performance quantity was calculated.",
